# foreman - local environment (example)

Copy to `LOCAL.md` beside SKILL.md and fill in. SKILL.md reads it when present; it is never committed.
Everything here is optional; with no LOCAL.md the foreman asks the owner and fills `defaults.yaml` per job.

## Worker routing

| Role | Worker | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| main builder | `<harness/model-version>` | e.g. an opencode or Claude Agent model |
| simple | `<model>` | |
| harder | `<model>` | |
| UI work | `<model>` | give it a mechanics-level brief |
| advisor | `<model>` | deepest thinker you have |
| milestone review | `<model>` | fallback `<model>` |
| contract stages | `<model>` | |

Concurrency limits (e.g. "only one opencode run at a time", "max 2 heavy agents").

## Accounts

Which account or key each harness uses, by env var NAME only. Never put a secret value here.

## Paths

Where your prototype and deployed copies live, where scorecards are logged, known tracker URLs.

## Owner conventions

Base branch, release rules, where review findings go.
